 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Rules are recorded on the bundle first, then replayed onto the app when the bundle is registered.\n\n1. **Recording (at definition time)**\n   - `Bundle.attach_route_rule` in `src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:413` validates the endpoint and view names. It does not touch the app.\n   - It calls `Bundle.record` (`bundles.py:224`) with a lambda, `lambda s: s.attach_route_rule(...)`. That appends the lambda to `self.deferred_functions`.\n\n2. **Registration**\n   - `App.register_bundle` in `src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571` just calls `bundle.register(self, options)`.\n   - `Bundle.register` in `src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:273`:\n     - checks the name is unique and stores the bundle in `app.bundles`.\n     - builds a `BundleSetupState` through `make_setup_state` (`bundles.py:246`), which carries the `url_prefix`, `subdomain` and `url_defaults`.\n     - replays every deferred lambda with `deferred(state)` (`bundles.py:334`). The static-file route goes through `state.attach_route_rule` the same way (`bundles.py:324`).\n\n3. **Applying to the app**\n   - `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` in `bundles.py:87`:\n     - prepends `url_prefix` to the rule.\n     - sets `subdomain` and merges `url_defaults`.\n     - prefixes the endpoint with `name_prefix.name.`.\n     - calls `self.app.attach_route_rule(...)` (`bundles.py:110`).\n   - `App.attach_route_rule` in `src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606` normalizes the methods and then builds the URL rule with the app's rule class (`url_rule_class`, around `app.py:252`). It then adds that rule to the app's URL map.",
